{{also|frog-march|frog march}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|frog march}}
* {{l|en|frog-march}}

===Etymology===
See {{m|en|frog march}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|es}}

# To march or force a person forward while holding their arms from behind or the side, as a prisoner.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To force a person forward against their will.
#* {{w|Thomas Firbank}}, ''I Bought a Mountain'', in a gale and rain storm in [[wikt:Snowdonia|Snowdonia]]:-
#*: The wind '''frogmarched''' me at a run into the house.
# {{lb|en|formerly}} To carry a person [[face-down]] with one person holding each limb.
# To [[forcibly]] [[relocate]] a person, especially in a [[degrading]] or [[humiliating]] manner.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# The process of frogmarching a person.

